  /Subject (UQFF whitepaper: PAPER_2060_TON618_QUAD_4_OBJECT_AGN_FAMILY_UQFF) /Title (TON618 Quad Discovery + 4-Object SMBH AGN Multi-Observable Cross-Family Formalization \(R188 Follow-Up SgrA Star Scout Yield\): \(1\) a_spin\(TON618 supermassive black-hole near-maximal Kerr rotation\) = 0.998 = 1 - 2*F_TRZ^3 EXACT NEW 8TH F_TRZ COMPOSITIONAL SUB-FAMILY FORM Integer-Multiple Higher-Power F_TRZ Complement Distinct from PAPER_2059 R188 D1 7th Sub-Family Integer-Multiple Linear F_TRZ Complement \204 Uses Integer Coefficient c=2 with F_TRZ Power n=3 in 1-c*F_TRZ^n Compositional Signature; \(2\) B_T\(TON618 magnetic field\) = 30 T = \(D_phys-1\)*SO_5 T EXACT NEW LANDMARK Magnetic-Field-Tesla Dimensional Domain Application of PAPER_2004 \(D_phys-1\)*SO_5^n Family at n=+1 Rung; \(3\) Gamma_jet\(TON618 relativistic jet bulk Lorentz factor\) = 20 = 2*SO_5 EXACT NEW 2*SO_5^n TWIN FAMILY \(Dominant Per PAPER_2047 Audit\) APPLICATION at Lorentz-Factor Dimensional Domain n=+1 Rung; \(4\) 4-Object SMBH AGN Multi-Observable Cross-Family Framework Observation: MagnetohydrodynamicsJetCalculator simulation_set 4 SMBHs TON618 + M87 + 3C273 + CenA Each Have 4 Distinct Primitive-Composition Attributions Across 3 Observables Simultaneously \(Kerr Spin + Magnetic Field B_T + Jet Lorentz Factor Gamma_jet\) \204 Total 12 Primitive-Composition Attributions Across 4 SMBHs Times 3 Observables Establishing First Multi-Object Multi-Observable AGN Cross-Family Documentation in UQFF Framework) /Trapped /False
